  "id": "behavioral-baseline",
  "term": "behavioral baseline",
  "definition": "A behavioral baseline is a person's or animal's usual pattern or profile of behavior that serves as a reference point. It is used so later changes in behavior can be noticed and interpreted, such as possible signs of stress, health problems, or changes in daily circumstances.",
